# Changelog

## [2.7.0] - 2026-11-09

### Added
- `keepQueryParams` config option (global and per-crawl) to preserve specific query parameters. All other query parameters are ignored by default when crawling, so `?a=1` and `?b=2` are treated as the same page.
- Crawl progress logging (fetched/discovered counts) so long crawls no longer appear frozen.

### Changed
- Screenshots are now captured with Puppeteer's native full-page mode instead of scrolling and stitching viewport segments. This removes scroll-position drift that shifted text between runs.
- Smooth scrolling is disabled during capture, and lazy content is loaded with a bounded scroll pass before the screenshot.
- `crawlMaxPages` now caps discovered pages. Previously only fetched pages were capped, so the number of pages to screenshot could far exceed the configured limit.
- `excludePathPattern` now skips fetching excluded URLs during crawling instead of only filtering the final page list.
- `closeBrowsers` now awaits browser shutdown and no longer throws when the browser pool count is inconsistent, allowing the process to exit cleanly.

### Fixed
- `includePathPattern` and `excludePathPattern` glob matching now handles `*` and `?` correctly. Previously `tag/*` was compiled to an invalid regex and never matched `tag/foo`.
- Screenshot comparison now reports differences when image dimensions differ instead of returning `0%`.
- Removed a potential hang caused by waiting for scroll settling via `requestAnimationFrame`, which Chrome throttles when the browser window is occluded or backgrounded.

## [2.6.0] - 2026-06-10

### Added
- Browser console log capture on every page (`console.*`, `pageerror` events).
- Failed page HTML dump (`.html`) alongside existing screenshot on failure.
- Failed page browser console log dump (`.log`) on failure.
- `enrichActionError` helper that attaches page URL, title, and last 20 console logs to action failure errors.

### Changed
- `wait` and `click` action failures now include enriched debug context (URL, title, console logs).
- `takeFailedPageScreenshot` refactored into focused helpers: `takeFailedPageScreenshot`, `saveFailedPageHtml`, `saveBrowserLogs`.
- Verbose logging enabled by default in config.

## [2.5.0] - 2026-05-05

### Added
- Configurable `captureFailedPage` and `failedScreenshotDir` to capture screenshots on failures.

## [2.4.0] - 2026-05-04

### Added
- Configurable sleep time between failed page retries (`failedSleepTimeMs`) to handle transient failures.

## [2.3.1] - 2026-03-25

### Fixed
- Wait action timeout is now configurable using the `globalSelectorTimeoutMs` config parameter.

## [2.3.0] - 2026-03-17

### Added
- Per-page watchdog timeout (`pageTimeoutMs`, default 5 minutes) to avoid hanging indefinitely.
- Non-verbose per-page progress logs with elapsed time.

### Changed
- HTML extra content is now provided as an inline string via `--html-extra` (file-based option removed).
- `withTimeout` helper moved to shared utils.

### Fixed
- Prevented unnecessary waiting when a free browser is already in the pool.

## [2.2.1] - 2026-03-13

### Added
- Per-crawl include/exclude path patterns (`includePathPattern`, `excludePathPattern`) to filter discovered URLs.

## [2.2.0] - 2026-03-12

### Added
- Configurable report mode (`reportMode`) to control whether all pages, only changed pages, or changed-first output is printed.
- Configurable diff image saving (`saveDiffs`) to control when diff images are written.
- Configurable retry count (`retryFailedPages`) for re-running failed page tests.

### Changed
- Page results output now supports changed-first reporting and respects the configured diff threshold when listing changed pages.

## [2.1.1] - 2026-03-11

### Changed
- Clicking now forces interaction even when elements are not visible to improve reliability.

## [2.1.0] - 2026-03-01

### Changed
- Output messages are now clearer.

## [2.0.0] - 2026-02-28

### Added
- Page crawling implementation.
- Run-and-email automation script.
- Verbose logging mode for execution tracing.

### Changed
- Screenshot capture stability improved with viewport fixes, timeout waits, and better animation handling.
- Root URL handling corrected.

### Fixed
- General error handling improvements and better runtime diagnostics.
- Console output cleanup (removed debug/noisy logs, added clearer info/error logs).

## [1.1.0] - 2026-02-27

### Added
- Baseline update status message output.
- Custom browser executable configuration, including `firefox-esr` support.
- Configurable config file path.
- Configurable timeouts for browser and screenshot operations.

## [1.0.0] - 2024-09-12

### Added
- First release.
